00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.310
Get it back to the ship.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:41.310
I want an analysis of their tactical systems as soon as possible.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:41.910
Awesome.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:57.930
Did you find their bridge?

00:07:58.970 --> 00:07:59.970
I'm not certain there is.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.620
Their command functions appear to be distributed through various...

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:04.680
Captain!

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:09.740
I'm all right.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:11.970
We should get you to sickbay.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:28.550
Neurotoxin, likely part of an autonomic defense system.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:29.800
The egg, probably.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.240
you a threat. Humans seem to have that effect on the Zindi. An analgesic should take care of the

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:44.670
irritation. Malcolm's bringing you two dead insectoids. I want you to learn as much as you

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:52.540
can about them. Understood. We've located their armory, found several particle weapons and torpedo

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:57.620
casings. What about the data you recovered? And since Otto's translating it, we'll be ready to

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.600
leave orbit as soon as the Zindi shuttle's aboard.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.410
Clear the thermosphere.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.010
We might want to do a better job securing our guests.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.710
I think it's safe to assume it's dead.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.340
Just being cautious.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.400
Certain insects on Earth are known to hibernate.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.490
You don't intend to shoot me, Major.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.350
It's not you I'm worried about.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:49.840
I've been going over the results from the last training session.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.450
Senior officers have shown a lot of improvement,

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:53.510
but I think they can do better.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.100
With your permission,

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.540
I'd like to schedule some more target practice for Monday evening.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:09:59.970
Won't go ever well with Command...

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:08.840
tucker monday night is movie night maybe he can sacrifice some leisure time for the sake of this

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:16.430
mission senior officers do have other duties we can't all spend our time playing holographic games

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:23.210
in the armory i'm not sure that's how the captain would see it eyes to shuttle pod two you're clear

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:27.590
to approach acknowledged deploy the docking arm

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.680
I think we figured out what happened to them.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.030
One of the nacelles fractured while they were coming out of a subspace vortex.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.910
They probably tried to make an emergency landing on this planet.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:49.090
According to Phlox, the insectoids we found weren't killed in the crash. They suffocated.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:53.300
Most of the crew appeared to have died when they transferred their life support to the hatchery.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.620
They sacrificed themselves to save their children.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.440
You said the hatchery's losing biosupport.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:04.080
