in their shields, not to play more games. This isn't exactly a game, Lieutenant. The simulation

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:15.870
found that they're vulnerable here. They've got minimal shielding around their impulse manifolds.

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:21.440
A pair of torpedoes should be enough to take out the engines. Those manifolds are pretty narrow,

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:29.850
but our targeting scanners should be able to get a lock. Let's work. Thank you, sir.

00:24:32.910 --> 00:24:36.350
